CAT = "bmGear"; SEG = "GEA"
Q = [
('Besides a helmet, what must a motorcycle rider wear in Belgium?',
 'Gloves, jacket, trousers, boots', ['A reflective vest only', 'Gloves and a spine protector only', 'A jacket and knee pads'],
 'The Highway Code requires riders and passengers to wear gloves, a long-sleeved jacket, trousers or overalls, and boots or ankle boots that protect the ankles.'),
('Your passenger wants to ride in shorts on a hot day. Under the Highway Code:',
 'Long trousers are required too', ['Shorts are fine for passengers', 'Shorts are fine below 50 km/h', 'Only the rider needs trousers'],
 'The clothing rule covers passengers as well as riders: gloves, a long-sleeved jacket, trousers or overalls and boots protecting the ankles.'),
("What must a motorcyclist's boots protect, under the Highway Code?",
 'The ankles', ['The knees', 'Only the toes', 'The shins up to the knee'],
 'Riders and passengers must wear boots or ankle boots that protect the ankles. Trainers that leave the ankle bare do not meet the rule.'),
('Which jacket meets the Highway Code rule for motorcycle riders?',
 'One with long sleeves', ['Any sleeveless vest', 'A short-sleeved shirt', 'A rain cape over a T-shirt'],
 'A long-sleeved jacket is required for the rider and the passenger, along with gloves, trousers or overalls, and ankle-protecting boots.'),
('You ride 300 m to the corner shop. Must you and your passenger wear helmets?',
 'Yes, on every ride', ['No, below 30 km/h', 'Only the rider must', 'Only outside built-up areas'],
 'Motorcycle riders and passengers must wear a protective helmet whenever they ride, whatever the distance or speed.'),
('You try on a helmet in a shop in Liège. Which sign shows it is right for you?',
 'Snug, does not shift when fastened', ['Loose, to keep your head cool', 'Tilted back to widen your view', 'Easy to pull off with the strap done up'],
 'A helmet that is loose or unfastened can come off in a crash. It should sit snugly without moving and be fastened every time.'),
('Your helmet slipped off the seat and struck a concrete floor. How should you treat it?',
 'As damaged: replace it', ['As fine if it still fits', 'Repaint the scuffed shell', 'Pad the dent with foam'],
 'A helmet absorbs one impact by crushing its inner liner, and the damage is often invisible. After a hard knock, replace it.'),
('Why replace a badly scratched visor?',
 'It scatters light and dazzles', ['It makes the helmet heavier', 'It lets in too much wind', 'It is only a cosmetic matter here'],
 'Scratches scatter the light of oncoming headlights and low sun, so you see less at exactly the moments you need to see most.'),
('You ride into the Kennedy tunnel in Antwerp with a dark visor down. What is the problem?',
 'You see far less inside', ['The visor will mist over', 'The tunnel lights glare', 'Nothing, tunnels are lit'],
 'A dark visor cuts the light reaching your eyes. In tunnels, at night or in dull weather it hides hazards, so use a clear visor.'),
('Which riding jacket makes you easiest to spot on a grey afternoon?',
 'A fluorescent yellow one', ['A black leather one', 'A dark green one', 'A navy textile one'],
 'Fluorescent colours stand out by day, even in dull light. At night, reflective material that bounces headlight beams back works far better.'),
('On an unlit road at night, what on your clothing shows up best in headlights?',
 'Reflective strips', ['Fluorescent fabric alone', 'A black helmet', 'A chrome-look visor'],
 'Fluorescent colours need daylight to glow. Reflective material shines back in headlight beams, so it shows you after dark.'),
('You plan to check tyre pressures straight after a 100 km ride. Why is that a poor time?',
 'Hot tyres read too high', ['Hot tyres read too low', 'The gauge will freeze', 'The valves are locked'],
 'Riding warms the air inside and raises the pressure, so a reading taken hot is misleading. Check before setting off, with the tyres cold.'),
('Your drive chain hangs very slack. What is the risk?',
 'It can jump off', ['The engine overheats', 'The brakes fade', 'The lights dim'],
 'A slack chain can jump the sprocket and lock the rear wheel or damage the engine casing. Adjust and lubricate it as the maker says.'),
("What do the tread wear indicators in a tyre's grooves show?",
 'The tyre is worn out', ['The tyre is under-inflated', 'The tyre was fitted backwards', 'The rim is bent'],
 'When the tread is worn level with the raised wear indicators, the tyre has reached its limit and must be replaced.'),
('Your front brake lever feels spongy and comes back towards the grip. What should you do?',
 'Get the brakes checked first', ['Pump it while riding', 'Use only the rear brake', 'Ride gently to the next service'],
 'A spongy lever can mean air in the hydraulics or low fluid, and the brake may fail when you need it. Do not ride until it is fixed.'),
('You forget to flick the side stand up and ride off. What can happen at the first left-hand bend?',
 'It digs in and levers the bike over', ['It drains the battery', 'It blocks the rear brake pedal', 'It stops the horn working'],
 'A side stand left down can hit the road when you lean left and lever the bike over. Many bikes cut the engine if you select a gear with it down.'),
('Which light should you check works when either brake is used?',
 'The brake light', ['The number plate light', 'The hazard lights', 'The main beam'],
 'Drivers behind rely on the brake light to know you are slowing. Check it lights with the front lever and with the rear pedal.'),
('On a long ride on the E411, what does constant wind noise in your helmet cause?',
 'Tiredness and hearing damage', ['Better concentration', 'Clearer engine sounds', 'Nothing, it is harmless'],
 'Wind noise in a helmet is loud enough to tire you and damage hearing over time. Earplugs cut the noise but still let you hear sirens and horns.'),
('Your rain suit is in the top box and it starts to pour. Why put it on?',
 'Cold and wet slow you down', ['It makes you go faster', 'It is only for your appearance', 'It protects the seat'],
 'Riding wet and cold drains your concentration and slows your reactions. Stop safely and put the waterproofs on.'),
('You borrow a friend\'s motorcycle. Why adjust the mirrors before you ride off?',
 'So they show the road behind you', ['So they catch less wind', 'So the bike may be parked legally', 'So they aim the headlight'],
 'Mirrors set for your riding position show the traffic behind you. Even so, a shoulder check is still needed for the blind spot.'),
]
